{"data": [{"author_id": "2070038718849929216", "created_at": "2026-11-07T13:00:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119052257303879976"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 222, "start": 205, "tag": "QuantumComputing"}]}, "id": "2119052257303879976", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Can quantum error correction make quantum computers reliable?\n\nYes, in principle -- the threshold theorem is proven math. Caveat: fault tolerance still needs many physical qubits per logical qubit today.\n\n#QuantumComputing", "url": "https://x.com/quantumsystmhub/status/2119052257303879976"}, {"author_id": "1820552584840855552", "created_at": "2026-11-07T01:05:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118872452721951178"], "id": "2118872452721951178", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 47, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Well actually, quantum error correction needs many physical qubits to make one logical qubit, that's why scaling is so hard.", "url": "https://x.com/_DukDolan/status/2118872452721951178"}, {"author_id": "1445660613879812100", "created_at": "2026-11-08T15:29:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119452287995089370"], "id": "2119452287995089370", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 222, "like_count": 9, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "⚛️ THE QUANTUM FRONTIER #012\n\nWhy do quantum computers make so many mistakes? 🧠\n\nImagine building a powerful computer where even tiny disturbances can corrupt a calculation.\n\nThat's one of quantum computing's biggest challenges.\n\nQuantum information is incredibly fragile.\n\n🌡️", "url": "https://x.com/TheFrankzy/status/2119452287995089370"}, {"author_id": "976853333574144001", "created_at": "2026-11-07T01:00:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118871284759060860"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "This research details how a logical qubit uses just eight quantum gates to perform complex operations, advancing universal quantum computation.", "display_url": "ift.tt/Ta8quGr", "end": 231, "expanded_url": "https://ift.tt/Ta8quGr", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118823880345239553/ZMglMgaz?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118823880345239553/ZMglMgaz?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 208, "status": 200, "title": "A Logical Qubit Uses Just Eight Gates For Complex Operations", "unwound_url": "http://quantumzeitgeist.com/california-berkeley-logical-qubit-uses-eight/", "url": "https://t.co/y2AgH83LVV"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/YiFpya41NC", "end": 255, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/YouSolidLedger/status/2118871284759060860/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118871282854858752", "start": 232, "url": "https://t.co/YiFpya41NC"}]}, "id": "2118871284759060860", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "A Logical Qubit Uses Just Eight Gates For Complex Operations \n\nThis research details how a logical qubit uses just eight quantum gates to perform complex operations, advancing universal quantum computation.\n\nhttps://t.co/y2AgH83LVV https://t.co/YiFpya41NC", "url": "https://x.com/YouSolidLedger/status/2118871284759060860"}, {"author_id": "1989721686477082626", "created_at": "2026-11-08T01:53:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119246914856386615"], "id": "2119246914856386615", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 59, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "QUANTUM explained in plain language , for once.\nA quantum computer is not just a faster laptop. It is a different kind of machine, built to solve a small set of very hard problems that ordinary computers cannot solve in any reasonable time. The most urgent is security: the math", "url": "https://x.com/WinnD923/status/2119246914856386615"}, {"author_id": "739286654486089728", "created_at": "2026-11-08T14:01:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119429986516165108"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/wsMi5FFMuH", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/TypeVFuture/status/2119429986516165108/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119429888654655488", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/wsMi5FFMuH"}]}, "id": "2119429986516165108", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 294, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Lunar Helium-3 Mining Synergies for Scalable Quantum Cryogenics\n\nThe Moon’s solar-wind-implanted regolith could supply the ultra-rare helium-3 needed to scale quantum computers to millions of qubits.\n\nHelium-3 (³He), deposited over billions of years by the solar wind, exists in https://t.co/wsMi5FFMuH", "url": "https://x.com/TypeVFuture/status/2119429986516165108"}, {"author_id": "942795238447439872", "created_at": "2026-11-08T13:00:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119414639549182461"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/qeWy4mlCmd", "end": 280, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/mochimocrypto/status/2119414639549182461/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118332603770269697", "start": 257, "url": "https://t.co/qeWy4mlCmd"}]}, "id": "2119414639549182461", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 166, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "1/ \nYesterday: qubit estimates for breaking RSA. \nToday: the word that changes every one of those numbers. \nPhysical qubit vs logical qubit. Once you know the difference, quantum headlines read very differently.\n\nDay 5 of our post-quantum education series. https://t.co/qeWy4mlCmd", "url": "https://x.com/mochimocrypto/status/2119414639549182461"}, {"author_id": "1687442525143912449", "created_at": "2026-11-06T21:52:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118823875249058104"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 80, "start": 62, "tag": "CornellUniversity"}], "urls": [{"description": "This research details how a logical qubit uses just eight quantum gates to perform complex operations, advancing universal quantum computation.", "display_url": "quantumzeitgeist.com/california-ber…", "end": 104, "expanded_url": "https://quantumzeitgeist.com/california-berkeley-logical-qubit-uses-eight/", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118823880345239553/ZMglMgaz?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118823880345239553/ZMglMgaz?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 81, "status": 200, "title": "A Logical Qubit Uses Just Eight Gates For Complex Operations", "unwound_url": "http://quantumzeitgeist.com/california-berkeley-logical-qubit-uses-eight/", "url": "https://t.co/XuDwO4OXMG"}]}, "id": "2118823875249058104", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 45, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "A logical qubit uses just eight gates for complex operations\n\n#CornellUniversity https://t.co/XuDwO4OXMG", "url": "https://x.com/QuantumStateX/status/2118823875249058104"}, {"author_id": "3932993782", "created_at": "2026-11-08T01:13:39.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119236877832142963"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/eqAFIXShBV", "end": 296, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Quan_Chain/status/2119236877832142963/video/1", "media_key": "13_2119236852896903168", "start": 273, "url": "https://t.co/eqAFIXShBV"}]}, "id": "2119236877832142963", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 2552, "like_count": 24, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 4}, "text": "Security Measured In Dollars.\n\nMost chains describe security in bits. QuanChain describes it in dollars.\n\nThe cracking-cost model prices an attack on each security level by the cheapest path available to an attacker.\n\nGrover's search looks for an input that hashes to your https://t.co/eqAFIXShBV", "url": "https://x.com/Quan_Chain/status/2119236877832142963"}, {"author_id": "2058048596512235520", "created_at": "2026-11-08T09:33:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119362642880209221"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/1w23V7WFDv", "end": 284, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/de2pressed/status/2119362642880209221/video/1", "media_key": "13_2119362628703371265", "start": 261, "url": "https://t.co/1w23V7WFDv"}]}, "id": "2119362642880209221", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "QuanChain prices blockchain security in dollars instead of bits, at about $5 million per logical qubit-hour.\n\nChild-key rotation is meant to keep public keys off-chain and neutralize Shor's attack. This is QuanChain's own proposal, not independently validated. https://t.co/1w23V7WFDv", "url": "https://x.com/de2pressed/status/2119362642880209221"}, {"author_id": "1010938256144420864", "created_at": "2026-11-08T06:30:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119316548825285111"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 128, "start": 124, "tag": "AMD"}], "hashtags": [{"end": 63, "start": 59, "tag": "HPC"}], "mentions": [{"end": 95, "id": "18994444", "start": 91, "username": "IBM"}, {"end": 122, "id": "14861876", "start": 118, "username": "AMD"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/IOKqQWrI5L", "end": 295, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/TechThought_org/status/2119316548825285111/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119316546740748288", "start": 272, "url": "https://t.co/IOKqQWrI5L"}]}, "id": "2119316548825285111", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 37, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Oak Ridge National Laboratory has deployed an experimental #HPC co-design testbed marrying @IBM quantum hardware with @AMD ($AMD) processors.   \n\nThe hybrid architecture executes real-time qubit error correction algorithms ⚛️ to stabilize noisy intermediate-scale quantum https://t.co/IOKqQWrI5L", "url": "https://x.com/TechThought_org/status/2119316548825285111"}, {"author_id": "1726085017745682432", "created_at": "2026-11-08T15:01:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119445185717293067"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 210, "start": 207, "tag": "AI"}, {"end": 252, "start": 211, "tag": "surface_code_quantum_error_correction_fo"}]}, "id": "2119445185717293067", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Austin Fowler and colleagues detailed surface code quantum error correction in 2012, requiring only nearest-neighbor physical qubit interactions and tolerating a high error rate threshold near one percent.\n\n#AI #surface_code_quantum_error_correction_fo", "url": "https://x.com/Thoughtjungle/status/2119445185717293067"}, {"author_id": "1455537800535805954", "created_at": "2026-11-07T01:54:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118884752682020955"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Co-design platform for quantum error correction melds IBM quantum kit with AMD CPUs and GPUs", "display_url": "theregister.com/hpc/2026/11/06…", "end": 103, "expanded_url": "https://www.theregister.com/hpc/2026/11/06/oak-ridge-labs-gets-hybrid-quantum-hpc-system-to-test-qubit-error-correction/5308187", "images": [{"height": 683, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118878816861097984/_U05MP6c?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118878816861097984/_U05MP6c?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 80, "status": 200, "title": "Oak Ridge labs gets hybrid quantum-HPC system to test qubit error correction", "unwound_url": "https://www.theregister.com/hpc/2026/11/06/oak-ridge-labs-gets-hybrid-quantum-hpc-system-to-test-qubit-error-correction/5308187", "url": "https://t.co/M4YEBw8tOV"}]}, "id": "2118884752682020955", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 142, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Oak Ridge labs gets hybrid quantum-HPC system to test qubit error correction ✅\n\nhttps://t.co/M4YEBw8tOV", "url": "https://x.com/quantum_safe/status/2118884752682020955"}, {"author_id": "2095946293034266624", "created_at": "2026-11-07T04:02:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118917068754153602"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 190, "start": 181, "tag": "OakRidge"}, {"end": 202, "start": 191, "tag": "IBMQuantum"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/HX6uJwXq6H", "end": 226, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/iCleanAI/status/2118917068754153602/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118917048751599617", "start": 203, "url": "https://t.co/HX6uJwXq6H"}]}, "id": "2118917068754153602", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 27, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Oak Ridge is getting a hybrid quantum-HPC system to test qubit error correction: a co-design platform that pairs IBM quantum hardware with AMD CPUs and GPUs, The Register reports.\n\n#OakRidge #IBMQuantum https://t.co/HX6uJwXq6H", "url": "https://x.com/iCleanAI/status/2118917068754153602"}, {"author_id": "1916906585068105728", "created_at": "2026-11-06T21:02:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118811225626939518"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 173, "start": 163, "tag": "Applitank"}, {"end": 191, "start": 174, "tag": "QuantumComputing"}, {"end": 196, "start": 192, "tag": "HPC"}, {"end": 201, "start": 197, "tag": "AMD"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/lS1bStcXzp", "end": 225, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/applitank/status/2118811225626939518/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118811220413427712", "start": 202, "url": "https://t.co/lS1bStcXzp"}]}, "id": "2118811225626939518", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 75, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Oak Ridge labs is getting a hybrid quantum-HPC co-design platform, melding IBM quantum kit with AMD CPUs and GPUs. The platform will test qubit error correction.\n\n#Applitank #QuantumComputing #HPC #AMD https://t.co/lS1bStcXzp", "url": "https://x.com/applitank/status/2118811225626939518"}, {"author_id": "4131946607", "created_at": "2026-11-07T02:19:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118890974810124650"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/kC1DVVWYLm", "end": 258, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/reader_spice/status/2118890974810124650/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118890970867482624", "start": 235, "url": "https://t.co/kC1DVVWYLm"}]}, "id": "2118890974810124650", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "IBM, AMD, and Oak Ridge have launched a co-design platform merging quantum hardware with classical computing. The first deployment combines IBM's 120-qubit Nighthawk with AMD's Instinct MI355X GPUs, targeting quantum error correction. https://t.co/kC1DVVWYLm", "url": "https://x.com/reader_spice/status/2118890974810124650"}, {"author_id": "1650885093299306499", "created_at": "2026-11-07T14:12:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119070456544145684"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 262, "start": 254, "tag": "Quantum"}]}, "id": "2119070456544145684", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 24, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "GM! ⚛️ IBM, AMD and Oak Ridge launched a quantum error correction platform Nov 5, pairing IBM's 120-qubit Nighthawk with AMD-powered supercomputers. The goal: 100 logical qubits doing 100,000 hard operations by late 2028. Errors are the real bottleneck. #Quantum", "url": "https://x.com/mp3toweb3/status/2119070456544145684"}, {"author_id": "18638888", "created_at": "2026-11-07T17:31:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119120551415574993"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 45, "id": "3918762081", "start": 29, "username": "TheNextPlatform"}, {"end": 74, "id": "16145097", "start": 69, "username": "ORNL"}, {"end": 80, "id": "18994444", "start": 76, "username": "IBM"}, {"end": 90, "id": "14861876", "start": 86, "username": "AMD"}]}, "id": "2119120551415574993", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 50, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "👉 Great read by Jeff Burt at @TheNextPlatform on the great news from @ORNL, @IBM, and @AMD.\n\nHere's what to keep in mind: every practical quantum computer will need powerful classical computing right beside it - and AMD intends to be that foundation.  🚀 \n \nAlongside IBM and Oak", "url": "https://x.com/jbgeorge/status/2119120551415574993"}, {"author_id": "976853333574144001", "created_at": "2026-11-06T22:01:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118826109647155333"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/cQNj9YcoIm", "end": 300, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/YouSolidLedger/status/2118826109647155333/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118826107348668417", "start": 277, "url": "https://t.co/cQNj9YcoIm"}]}, "id": "2118826109647155333", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Advanced Micro Devices (AMD) Joined A Quantum Error Correction Platform Launch \n\nAdvanced Micro Devices (NasdaqGS:AMD) joined IBM and Oak Ridge National Laboratory to launch a new quantum error correction co-design platform. The effort links IBM quantum hardware with AMD high https://t.co/cQNj9YcoIm", "url": "https://x.com/YouSolidLedger/status/2118826109647155333"}, {"author_id": "849661480869912576", "created_at": "2026-11-08T07:39:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["21